@flexiarg hygiene/route-to-who-can-act
@title Route Each Finding To Whoever Can Act On It, With A Deadline
@keywords routing, escalation, handoff, warrant, queue, deferral, hygiene
@audience hygiene-policy authors, coordination designers, readers learning the library's layers
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; shared across the hygiene generations — see hygiene/README.md; the buffer cleaner has no instance yet)
@references [inbox-zero/escalate-by-who-can-act test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff hygiene/receipt-then-gate hygiene/settle-with-meters]
@see-also apparatus/every-wait-has-a-deadline
@why a finding that goes to a queue waits, and waiting work decays: the Street Sweeper's 2,551 correct patches went to an operator review queue on 2026-05-25 and three months later 0 of 60 sampled still applied. A finding that goes nowhere is lost the same way. The finding has to reach a party who can act on it, carrying what that party needs.
@how every generation must: (1) resolve the nearest party able to act (the responsible seat, a peripheral, the operator only for judgement a person must make); (2) deliver exactly to that party with the evidence it needs to act (warrant ids, base sha, the differing fields); (3) set a deadline after which the finding acts or is re-routed; (4) type findings that arrive without their evidence (:unwarranted) rather than dropping or silently redoing them; (5) never route by volume alone to the operator.
@violation-signature inbox zero: Street Sweeper queue (2,551 patches, 0/60 applicable after three months); p4ng reached 291 unpushed commits because outlier escalation only runs inside agent-chat turn-end promotion, which the sessions writing p4ng never trigger (2026-09-16). Test registry: every WM review on 2026-09-16 received base shas but no warrant ids, and reran the author's tests (e.g. 86 tests on futon2 cb5f8b1288).
! conclusion: Findings are delivered to the nearest party able to act, with the evidence needed to act and a deadline; nothing is routed to a queue that waits.

  + context: Hygiene findings arrive continuously across agents and boxes; the operator's attention is the scarcest resource.

  + IF:
    A policy produces a finding it cannot act on itself.

  + HOWEVER:
    Routing to the operator builds a waiting queue; routing without evidence makes the recipient redo the work; and the responsible party may have left.

  + THEN:
    Resolve the acting party, deliver with evidence and a deadline, and type evidence-less handoffs.

  + BECAUSE:
    Does the output act, or does it wait? If it waits, it silts up at the rate work arrives.

  + evidence: As in the violation signatures. Gap: the buffer cleaner has no instance — its execution is refused until a gated consumer exists, so it has no findings to route yet. That absence is recorded here rather than filled with an invented instance.
